WEBVTT

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.070
The following tale is a work of pure fiction.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.940
<b>Would You Die for a Teakettle!? {ts}</b>

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.650
<b>August 1577 {ts}</b>

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.650
<b>Omi Province Azuchi Castle {ts top to bottom}</b>

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.460
Now that I, Furuta Sasuke, have reached 34 years of life,

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.310
what does the future behold?

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.440
Born into the era of the Warring States as a warrior,

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.690
I serve He, whose name has reached furthest corners of our land.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.740
He, who has grasped fame by subjugating the many provinces of the East.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:52.690
Even the Emperor bestows upon Milord, Oda Nobunaga, the famed agarwood, Ranjatai! {until no you ni}

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.710
Oh, Ranjatai...

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.060
I desire it!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.760
I-I desire the masterpiece so!

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:12.270
I must say, those barbarian garments Milord adorns are striking.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.480
The brilliance of "velvet" cloth {until nuno ni}

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.100
adorned by thinned arabesque tree peonies

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.780
leaves me in awe of it's sheer beauty.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.340
'Tis a garment which indeed is fitting Milord.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:31.040
The display of his vassals, by comparison, are defeated by a lack of originality.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:38.330
Take this oafish, seemingly pea-brained general for example.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.050
Were I this man, I would revert to the Muromachi period of armaments. {until aratame sasete}

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.740
A Deva breastplate, and scale armor for spaulders and vambraces shall suffice. {until kobire no}

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:52.060
Such revisions shall display these generals as elite warriors of our army.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.060
How pitiful.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.410
This man's attire are updated to say, and yet he seems profoundly despondent.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:05.620
Were I him, "cowardice" shall be written upon my plate as a display for all,

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:04.350
Sasuke. {oda}

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.610
should a pathetic death ever deprive me of my "cowardice." {until wakaranu mi}

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:13.290
The corpse would be so unsightly, even bandits would cry with laughter.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.260
Sasuke. {oda}

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:14.080
Sasuke!

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.960
What amuses you so?

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:19.670
Is it death you desire?!

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:20.680
Nay! {hah}

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:24.670
Does his property and stipend of 200 koku amuse him so?

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:30.140
Nay, but his young wife of twenty surely amuses him so.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.590
Indeed, 'tis the uncouth laughter befitting of boorish warriors.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:42.010
Such humiliating laughter does only but ruin one's pride.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.690
I shall restrain myself henceforth.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:48.700
You have served me for 17 years, aye?

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:49.710
Aye.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:54.040
I serve as field messenger to relay Milord's absolute orders.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:58.960
I have relayed Milord's orders to our rear forces, and to the main camps of our foes.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:02.970
Now, I require such a task of you once more.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.050
Milord?

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.220
As you may know, the cunning old fox, Matsunaga Hisahide,

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.610
has betrayed me, once again.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:17.560
Betrayed, knowing the Uesugi forces of the North intend an invasion of our capital.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:26.060
He has joined with the Mori Clan and Ikko-ikki of the West, and hides in Shigisan Castle.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.750
I've sent messengers to Shigisan, but they've been refused an audience.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.490
Therein, we must lay siege upon the castle.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.410
And my orders, Milord?

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:40.580
My son, Nobutada, shall lead this expedition.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:47.870
Once Shigisan has been surrounded, you are to negotiate with Matsunaga.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.880
Tell him that his betrayal shall be forgiven, in exchange for the Hiragumo teakettle.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.220
Hiragumo?!

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.400
The legendary teakettle, Hiragumo?!

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.360
The very teakettle rumored to resemble a spider crawling on the ground?!

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.590
That masterpiece, the Hiragumo?!

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.840
Enough with your illustrative appraisals!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.400
Have your eyes ever captured its visage?

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:11.000
Nay, Milord.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.120
My eyes have naught the capacity to behold such a treasure.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.660
Ever the aesthete, alike your father.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:22.640
He was my most valued tea master...

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.970
Now, go and smoke the old fox off of the mountain.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.920
I shan't allow any further delays!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.480
Sasuke.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:37.920
Yes...

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.680
General Hashiba Hideyoshi?

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:45.190
Is the teakettle such a masterpiece, as you say?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.430
Indeed it is, General.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:49.690
Curiosity? {sore ga nani ka}

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:56.920
No, I merely thought that I'd be hearing Milord's shrill laughter soon.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.750
<b>October 1577 {ts}</b>

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.750
<b>Yamato Province Shigisan Castle {ts}</b>

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:04.140
I come bearing a message from Oda Nobunaga!

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.300
I am Furuta Sasuke, a field messenger of Oda Nobunaga!

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:25.660
I come to express Milord's desire for negotiations!

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:28.020
Open the gate!

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:33.740
Milord, the enemy sends a field messenger.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:53.570
At last, I may gaze upon the splendor of legend. {until kono mede}

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:59.420
Although, it is uncertain whether General Matsunaga keeps it in plain view.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.900
Think naught of the teakettle!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.290
I only desire to fulfill my orders as a warrior.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.080
Henceforth, I shall think only of success!

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:26.060
Milord grants amnesty towards General Matsunaga's betrayal... {until jouken wa}

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:33.230
in exchange for the legendary teakettle, the Hira...

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.280
Hiragu-! {until hiragu}

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:57.170
The Hiragumo is my very soul!

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:03.630
To relinquish my soul is to relinquish my life.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.680
I shan't relinquish my soul to none!

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.050
T-There it is!

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:11.180
Before my very eyes!

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:15.460
I have done terrible deeds to survive these chaotic times. {until ikinuitekita}

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.930
I've ended the life of Shogun Ashikaga Yoshiteru, destroyed the Great Buddha of Nara, {until yaki}

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:22.510
and I've taken all that, which my heart desires so.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.450
My fate is my own.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:28.970
The design and pattern are simply captivating.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:33.460
The mere symmetry, no, the embossedness of the piece is marvelous.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:39.960
The Sixth Demon Lord is too merciful, once more allowing amnesty for my rebellious ways. {until mata yurusuto}

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:44.460
Though tea master, Yamanoue Souji, decrees the Hiragumo a useless treasure,

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:46.470
has his eyes ever captured the teakettle itself?! {until mita no ka}

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:50.020
Does Nobunaga wish to prolong my life so?

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:53.600
Or, perhaps he wishes to see my death, personally.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:58.980
Perhaps the teakettle possesses my very eyes!

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.640
Hear me, whelp!

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.320
An aesthete, are ye?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.890
I am a warrior. {until bujin}

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.590
Alike yourself, General, {matsunagasama douyou}

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:18.350
I am but another ambitious upstart. {until de gozaru}

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:50.530
The time shall come when you must choose

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:59.660
whether or not to follow in my footsteps against a force which overwhelms your own. {until washi no michi erabuka}

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:02.050
Or, shall you choose to serve your foes?

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:12.710
What is it?!

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.110
Sasuke, you may leave us now.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:35.320
I shall deal with the General.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.640
You've returned at last.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:57.700
Aye.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.120
What of Matsunaga's decision?

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:01.160
He declines Milord's offer of reconciliation.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:05.530
General Hashiba's warriors had infiltrated the castle shortly afterwards.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.360
Hideyoshi has?!

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.930
I gave no such order!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.870
Milord, the main gate!

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:14.080
General Hashiba's forces have left the castle!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:28.660
Is that...! {are wa}

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:29.970
Behold, the keep!

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.250
Nobunaga!

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.880
I shall await ye in Nirvana.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:57.870
C-Could he have filled the Hiragumo with gunpowder?!

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:02.830
On your deathbed, hold onto my old gift, the Tsukumonasu teacup,

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:08.920
and return it to me in Nirvana!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.060
Could it be...!

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.030
It burns!

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:10.440
<b> ...Later {ts}</b>

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:10.440
<b> Omi Province Azuchi Castle Grounds {ts}</b>

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:30.590
Milord, I've returned from Shigisan.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:38.840
'Tis most unfortunate to report... {until zonjimasuru}

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:41.090
General Matsunaga took the teakettle with him in death.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.130
I am very impressed with Milord's true intentions, {until sasshimasu suru tokoro}

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:51.530
for Milord's aim was never to attain Hiragumo.

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:54.070
Explain your impression.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:58.950
Milord's true desire was the heart of General Matsunaga.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:03.660
Though Milord and Matsunaga together have conquered many a great foe,

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:07.960
Milord's desire for the teakettle was a test of his loyalty.

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:14.380
Dare you to believe a simian may presume my intentions?!

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:21.460
I present to Milord, the last poem of Matsunaga Hisahide.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:32.400
"Were the World only greater, neither may have met. {until nakattarou ni}

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:38.910
And so, comrade, I compose naught but regret."

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:50.440
Crafty, is your simian wit!

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.290
Indeed, Milord!

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:57.380
I am but simian in nature. {until shosen saru}

00:16:57.380 --> 00:17:02.250
Laugh, for my human appearance covers my simian nature!

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:03.680
I shall leave.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:12.450
Simian.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.290
You shall lead our forces against the Mori clan.

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:25.200
Do return our losses to them.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:33.800
I am surprised he composed and recited his final poem, given his remaining time.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.710
'Twas mere child's play.

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:39.960
His followers would be beheaded had he refused to recite it. {until kiraseru}

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:43.100
As he had conceded, he was allowed to end his own life.

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:48.910
The pompous old fox would have done so, regardless.

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:51.810
If so, why compose a poem of reconcile?

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.600
I was the one who composed it.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:16.170
Milord, I present you with pieces of the Hiragumo.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.210
'Tis a pile of scrap iron.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:21.170
Nay, 'tis the lid of the Hiragumo.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.970
'Tis most unfortunate for a masterpiece to be reduced to pieces.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:52.710
Retrieved the skin of a roasting chestnut, have you?

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:56.210
Your desire for the teakettle was greater than my own!

00:18:57.850 --> 00:18:59.090
You may have it.

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.050
Now, leave me. {motteike}

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.710
Oh, the hilarity.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:17.020
Perhaps his life may not end as a mere field messenger.

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:54.630
It does not feel the same!

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.770
It looks too different!

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:02.650
Osen?

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:06.400
<b> 1578 {ts}</b>

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:06.400
<b> Izumi Province Sakai {ts}</b>

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:15.160
I-Is this truly a vessel?! {until kore wa}

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:21.670
The immenseness of this vessel is akin to the floating Ryugu Palace of myth!

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:33.680
Kuki Yoshitaka, 'tis a splendid vessel.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.860
The Great Atakebune intrigues me.

00:20:36.430 --> 00:20:38.450
Construct more, as I grant you leeway with the treasury.

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:43.470
We shall sink the minuscule vessels of Mori's navy!

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:48.910
I've left the castle with a mount to join Milord in surveying the new vessel.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:50.900
Always the aesthete.

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:56.790
I had naught a thought of it's immenseness...

00:20:56.790 --> 00:21:00.290
I desire only articles of grandeur.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:03.670
As do we all, had we the gold.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:09.410
Do forgive me.

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:12.180
'Tis merely the foolish prattle of a merchant.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:30.030
Speak your truth, but never recede.

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:37.160
What of your truth, Sasuke?

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:43.560
The Hiragumo pales to the immenseness of the vessel, aye?

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:19.340
Truthfully, Milord...

00:22:21.410 --> 00:22:26.460
size and virtue are of different schools.

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:37.810
The Hiragumo teakettle and Great Atakebune
are of equal grandeur.

00:24:34.760 --> 00:24:36.380
<b>Suppleness {ts}</b>

00:24:40.090 --> 00:24:41.720
<b>My karma is greater than his {ts}</b>

00:24:48.810 --> 00:24:50.480
<b>I find painting the vessel black to be most suitable {ts}</b>

00:24:50.490 --> 00:24:52.550
Next time, "Fantasy of the Tea Room."

00:24:52.980 --> 00:24:58.260
Does the fork joining the warrior and aesthete truly exist?

00:24:56.610 --> 00:24:59.770
<b>Fantasy of the Tea Room {ts}</b>
